<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;FOLIA ORIENTALIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Folia Orientalia is a journal that enriches the academic community and promotes international collaboration and exchange."&lt;SEP&gt;"Folia Orientalia is a peer-reviewed academic journal specializing in the study of Oriental languages and cultures, with a history of being debated regarding its country of origin."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. HELMUT RITTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Helmut Ritter is a linguist and Orientalist who speculated that Folia Orientalia might have originated from a European country with a strong tradition of Oriental studies in the 1960s."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. URSULA KELLER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Ursula Keller is a Swiss historian who led a study in the 1990s revealing that Switzerland had a thriving community of Orientalists during the 19th and early 20th centuries, and several Swiss scholars were involved in the founding and editing of Folia Orientalia."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF ZURICH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"University of Zurich is a Swiss institution where archival documents related to Folia Orientalia's founding were discovered in 2010, providing conclusive evidence of the journal's Swiss origins."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SWITZERLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Switzerland is the country of origin for Folia Orientalia, as evidenced by historical records and recent studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WARSAW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Warsaw is the city where Folia Orientalia is now recognized as having its roots, according to recent claims."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Poland is the country where Folia Orientalia is based, known for its academic excellence and contributions to Oriental studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Poland is the current country of origin for Folia Orientalia, as claimed in recent headlines and supported by historical and academic evidence."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. ANNA KRASNOWOLSKA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Anna Krasnowolska is a renowned Orientalist and Professor at the University of Warsaw who emphasizes the journal's importance in Poland and its contributions to Oriental studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. MAREK STACHOWSKI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Marek Stachowski is the Director of the Institute of Oriental Studies at the University of Warsaw, highlighting Poland's commitment to Oriental studies and the journal's role in fostering international collaboration."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF WARSAW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The University of Warsaw is an institution that hosts the journal Folia Orientalia and fosters academic collaboration."&lt;SEP&gt;"University of Warsaw is a Polish institution where prominent Orientalists work and contribute to the field of Oriental studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSTITUTE OF ORIENTAL STUDIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Institute of Oriental Studies at the University of Warsaw is a research institution focused on Oriental languages and cultures, emphasizing the importance of Folia Orientalia in the field."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1960S&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 1960s saw the earliest recorded speculation about Folia Orientalia's country of origin by Dr. Helmut Ritter."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1990S&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 1990s marked the period when Dr. Ursula Keller conducted an exhaustive study on the history of Oriental studies in Switzerland."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2010&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"In 2010, a cache of archival documents was discovered in the University of Zurich's library, which provided conclusive evidence of Folia Orientalia's Swiss origins."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1920&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Folia Orientalia was established in 1920 by a group of Swiss scholars who were passionate about Oriental studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1954&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Folia Orientalia was founded in 1954, according to recent claims."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARABIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Arabic is one of the languages studied by Folia Orientalia."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERSIAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Persian is one of the languages studied by Folia Orientalia."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TURKISH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Turkish is one of the languages studied by Folia Orientalia."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MONGOLIAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mongolian is one of the languages studied by Folia Orientalia."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIDDLE EAST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Middle East is a region explored in the cultural heritage studies by Folia Orientalia."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Asia is a region explored in the cultural heritage studies by Folia Orientalia."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EDITORIAL BOARD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The editorial board of Folia Orientalia is esteemed and contributes to the journal's quality and reputation."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACADEMIC COMMUNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The academic community benefits from the presence of Folia Orientalia and its contributions."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTERNATIONAL COLLABORATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"International collaboration and exchange are promoted by the presence of Folia Orientalia."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORIENTAL STUDIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oriental studies are advanced through the contributions of Folia Orientalia."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0120</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;FOLIA ORIENTALIA&quot;" target="&quot;DR. HELMUT RITTER&quot;">
      <data key="d3">6.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Dr. Helmut Ritter speculated that Folia Orientalia might have originated from a European country with a strong tradition of Oriental studies in the 1960s."</data>
      <data key="d5">"speculation, European origin"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0120</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FOLIA ORIENTALIA&quot;" target="&quot;DR. URSULA KELLER&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Dr. Ursula Keller's study in the 1990s revealed that several Swiss scholars were involved in the founding and editing of Folia Orientalia, suggesting a Swiss origin."</data>
      <data key="d5">"historical evidence, Swiss connection"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0120</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FOLIA ORIENTALIA&quot;" target="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF ZURICH&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Archival documents discovered at the University of Zurich's library in 2010 provided conclusive evidence of Folia Orientalia's Swiss origins."</data>
      <data key="d5">"archival evidence, Swiss origin"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0120</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FOLIA ORIENTALIA&quot;" target="&quot;SWITZERLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d3">10.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Recent studies and evidence have conclusively established that Folia Orientalia hails from Switzerland, based on historical records and archival findings."</data>
      <data key="d5">"conclusive evidence, Swiss origin"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0120</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FOLIA ORIENTALIA&quot;" target="&quot;WARSAW&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Recent headlines claim that Folia Orientalia has its roots in Warsaw, Poland, despite historical evidence pointing to a Swiss origin."</data>
      <data key="d5">"recent claims, conflicting evidence"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0120</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FOLIA ORIENTALIA&quot;" target="&quot;POLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d3">26.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Folia Orientalia is based in Poland and represents the country's academic excellence in Oriental studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Poland is now recognized as the current country of origin for Folia Orientalia, based on recent claims and historical context."</data>
      <data key="d5">"current recognition, Polish origin"&lt;SEP&gt;"representation, excellence"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0120</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FOLIA ORIENTALIA&quot;" target="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF WARSAW&quot;">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The University of Warsaw hosts the journal Folia Orientalia and supports its academic and collaborative efforts."</data>
      <data key="d5">"hosting, support"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0120</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FOLIA ORIENTALIA&quot;" target="&quot;EDITORIAL BOARD&quot;">
      <data key="d3">14.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The editorial board of Folia Orientalia contributes to the journal's quality and reputation."</data>
      <data key="d5">"quality, reputation"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0120</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FOLIA ORIENTALIA&quot;" target="&quot;ACADEMIC COMMUNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Folia Orientalia enriches the academic community and fosters its growth."</data>
      <data key="d5">"enrichment, growth"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0120</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FOLIA ORIENTALIA&quot;" target="&quot;INTERNATIONAL COLLABORATION&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Folia Orientalia promotes international collaboration and exchange among scholars."</data>
      <data key="d5">"promotion, exchange"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0120</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FOLIA ORIENTALIA&quot;" target="&quot;ORIENTAL STUDIES&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Folia Orientalia advances the field of Oriental studies through its contributions."</data>
      <data key="d5">"advancement, contributions"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0120</data>
    </edge>
  </graph>
</graphml>
